endobj
1300 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (A dual axis line chart extends the capabilities of a standard line chart by allowing two different sets of data to be plotted on the same chart with separate y-axes that share the same x-axis. This type of chart is beneficial when comparing two variables that have different scales or units of measurement but are related to the same x-axis values \(e.g., time periods\). By using dual axes, it becomes easier to identify and analyze trends, correlations, and discrepancies between the two datasets.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
