/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (A scatterplot is a type of diagram that uses Cartesian coordinates to display values for typically two variables for a set of data. Each dot in the scatterplot represents a single observation where the position on the x-axis and y-axis corresponds to the values of the two variables. Scatterplots are particularly useful for visually identifying relationships or correlations between variables, such as examining how changes in one variable affect another. They are effective in highlighting patterns, clusters, and outliers within the data.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
